    "::: {.try-this}\n",
    "Both metrics fall as $\\alpha$ rises — the method is straining to keep up with a trend it was never built for. After the first month every error is *positive*: the forecast is late as soon as the trend takes hold. **Persistent one-signed errors are the diagnostic that you need a trend model, not a better $\\alpha$.**\n",
